  "notes": [
    "Scope is a source audit and design proposal only; no service implementation, installer, tests, build, network or live database command executed.",
    "Expected next accepted baseline is supplied by parent report review: commit 0cb3484675ac9267a0f9d7f52f6e3dbff5074d1a, tree 6d213969675d86eea8e2ff56b99f9a232715b3a8, 2202 files. Parent owns complete acceptance/report verification.",
    "The audited 0cb3484 source tree CURRENT_STATE contains the package preparation checkpoint; the separate acceptance overlay updates that checkpoint. These source-tree continuity files are pinned as audited history, not a command to rerun the accepted package. SERVICE_ACCESS is dated 2026-10-27 and is not current deployment proof.",
    "A private helper change alone removes service cards but leaves both service profile envelopes profile_available=true and identity_id populated for an otherwise active identity. Early profile gates are therefore part of the same proposed bounded module.",
    "Do not modify is_public: it also gates new contacts, media bindings and provider target resolution. These semantics and existing replay/history remain separate work.",
    "Read fences do not alter service_role direct table privileges, BYPASSRLS, owner writes, existing public Storage URLs, already downloaded content or all account lifecycle paths.",
    "No million-user readiness claim: service search still builds a materialized eligible candidate set and exact total before pagination; arbitrary token substring filters and lower(city/country) are not proven to use the baseline discovery index.",
    "Fresh next-package verification must confirm exact new baseline Git/worktree/index/remote/dependencies, previous original receipt and current catalog before writes; released packages and logs remain immutable."
